{
    "background_story": "Princeton was a small, energetic sparrow who lived in a bustling forest filled with towering trees. As a member of the Emberizidae family, he was known for his striking plumage and impressive song. Princeton spent his days flitting between branches, searching for seeds and insects to fuel his active lifestyle. But what set him apart from his fellow sparrows was his remarkable ability to mimic the calls of other birds. Princeton could reproduce the sweet melodies of the orioles, the chirping of the finches, and even the haunting hoots of the owls. His talent earned him the nickname 'The Forest Maestro,' and birds from far and wide would gather to hear him sing. Princeton's Emberizidae heritage had gifted him with a remarkable voice, and he used it to bring joy and harmony to the forest community.",
